WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.906
OpenSSL patches a

00:00:01.718 --> 00:00:03.557
critical base64 buffer

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.135
overflow

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:06.218
A public OpenSSL

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.268
pull request fixes

00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:11.230
CVE-2026-121481

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:12.562
a buffer overflow

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:13.341
in the EVP

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:14.992
Encode Block base64

00:00:14.803 --> 00:00:15.499
encoder

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.209
rated 9.8 out

00:00:17.021 --> 00:00:17.669
of 10

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.333
The fix rejects

00:00:19.145 --> 00:00:20.135
NULL buffers

00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:21.527
negative lengths and

00:00:21.386 --> 00:00:22.741
inputs whose encoded

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:23.590
size would not

00:00:23.402 --> 00:00:24.003
fit in an

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:24.440
int

00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:25.587
It adds a

00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:26.377
similar guard to

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.615
EVP Decode Block

00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:28.676
fixes a bad

00:00:28.488 --> 00:00:29.242
length check in

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:30.516
the HTTP client's

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.966
base64 encoder

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:32.815
and adds new

00:00:32.627 --> 00:00:33.252
tests

00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:35.410
across branches 4.0

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:36.601
and 4.1

00:00:37.134 --> 00:00:38.148
Full story on

00:00:37.959 --> 00:00:38.855
the dashboard
